```ADD_PAPER
2505.03332v4
In "AI-Driven Scholarly Peer Review via Persistent Workflow Prompting, Meta-Prompting, and Meta-Reasoning," the authors present a framework that leverages advanced prompt engineering and meta-prompting mechanisms to enable LLMs to perform detailed scholarly reviews. Their approach uses a persistent workflow that guides the model through hierarchical reasoning and modular analysis, successfully extracting and evaluating quality signals from peer reviews. Extensive experiments demonstrate that this method not only identifies key methodological issues and evidentiary support within submissions but also aligns closely with expert assessments. These findings highlight the potential of using systematic, prompt-driven workflows to enhance a two-stage process—where initial reviewer comments are iteratively refined through targeted author feedback—thereby underpinning reviewer incentive systems in AI conferences. This paper provides critical insights into developing robust, reasoning-based techniques for accurate peer-review quality measurement.
```ADD_PAPER
``` 
